// // =============================================================
// // Module G: Notifications
// // =============================================================
// // Targeting collapses into two independent dimensions instead of a long
// // enum list: WHO receives it (student or parent) and HOW the audience is
// // selected (everyone, by group(s), or an explicit list). The audience is
// // then resolved into concrete NotificationRecipient rows at send time, so
// // if a student later leaves a group, the historical record of who was
// // actually notified doesn't silently change.
// //
// // Mapping of your five scenarios (same shape for recipientType = parent):
// //   Specific group      -> audienceScope = groups,       audienceFilter = {"groupIds":[15]}
// //   All groups          -> audienceScope = all,           audienceFilter = null
// //   N specific students -> audienceScope = individuals,   audienceFilter = {"ids":[45,46,47]}
// //   All students         -> audienceScope = all,           audienceFilter = null
// //   One specific student -> audienceScope = individuals,   audienceFilter = {"ids":[45]}

